/P 230 0 R
/T (The third medical camp was held in Rahim Yar Khan City, providing free healthcare services to approximately 600 individuals, including women, children, elderly residents, poor and needy people, and families requiring urgent medical support. As the largest camp under this initiative, it delivered extensive medical consultations, health assessments, treatment for common illnesses, and distribution of essential medicines. By bringing qualified medical professionals directly into the community, the camp significantly reduced healthcare barriers and enabled early diagnosis, timely treatment, and practical health guidance for underserved populations.)
/E (The third medical camp was held in Rahim Yar Khan City, providing free healthcare services to approximately 600 individuals, including women, children, elderly residents, poor and needy people, and families requiring urgent medical support. As the largest camp under this initiative, it delivered extensive medical consultations, health assessments, treatment for common illnesses, and distribution of essential medicines. By bringing qualified medical professionals directly into the community, the camp significantly reduced healthcare barriers and enabled early diagnosis, timely treatment, and practical health guidance for underserved populations.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
